// CONTRACT BEAT (seeded by the lead; owned by east): hands over hmCut
// (portvoltTree gate, with the Tide Badge). Every way of helping the
// captain ends with the disc.

## The cabin

::bg{location="captains-cabin" time="day"}
::auto{character="captainOrla" anchor="center" action="enter"}
@narrator: The captain's cabin smells of brass polish and misery. Captain Orla is green, and holding onto the desk with both hands.
@captainOrla{emotion="sad"}: Ugh. Thirty years at sea, and the sea and I have never once agreed. Who let you in?

<branch id="eastOrlaHelp" prompt="The captain looks terrible.">
  <choice id="rub" label="Rub the captain's back">
    @narrator: You rub the captain's back in small circles, the way Mom used to.
    @captainOrla: Oh. Oh, that's... that's actually helping. Keep going. Left a bit.
  </choice>
  <choice id="water" label="Fetch a glass of water">
    @narrator: You fetch a glass of water from the galley. The cook gives you a biscuit for the captain too.
    @captainOrla: Dry biscuit. The only cure that ever worked. How did you know?
  </choice>
  <choice id="horizon" label="Tell the captain to look at the horizon">
    @narrator: You open the porthole. The coast of Eastmarch is a steady grey line.
    @captainOrla: Look at the horizon. Every cabin boy tells me that. It works every time, and I forget every time.
  </choice>
</branch>

@captainOrla{emotion="happy"}: Ha! Better. You're a good kid.
@captainOrla: Here. When I was your age I cut hedges for a living with my old monster, before I ran off to sea like a fool. Now yours can cut them.
::use{component="obtain" item="hmCut"}
@captainOrla: The Tide Badge lets you use it outside battle. There's a tree on the Portvolt road that the council has been meaning to cut for a year. Go and embarrass them.
